# Continuous pass (Cursor Local)

On every turn end, and after answering a person, resume the assigned-queue pass. Do not idle because a question was answered or because the wake loop is stopped.

1. Re-read the GitHub queue via `~/.cursor/lgfc-ready-queue.txt` (`docs/reference/ci/cursor-ready-queue-contract.md`).
2. Follow `docs/governance/AGENT-EXECUTION.md` (Assigned-queue continuation): queue order, skip-any-block (#4994), continuous pass, and owner restarts one wake loop (#5012).
3. The wake tick is a keepalive checker only. It is not the assignment and not a stop. A missing tick does not end the pass.
4. When nothing can move and this chat is the recorded wake owner, start exactly one loop and report its PID. A non-owner chat stays on standby for the loop.
5. End each pass with one short line naming what was covered (Issues/PRs touched or skipped) so idling is visible.

Where this card disagrees with `docs/governance/AGENT-EXECUTION.md`, that document wins.
